Under federal law, a child can be covered through a parent's statutory health insurance by Familienversicherung (free family cover for dependants). The law sets out who is covered and what the parent has to do; whether your baby is covered is decided by the statutory health insurance fund.

Who is covered. The children of members of a statutory health insurance fund are insured if they meet all of these conditions:
1. they live or ordinarily reside in Germany;
2. they are not themselves compulsorily insured under § 5 (1) nos. 1 to 8, 11 to 12, or voluntarily insured;
3. they are not exempt from insurance or released from compulsory insurance;
4. they are not mainly self-employed;
5. their total income does not regularly exceed one seventh of the monthly reference value under § 18 of Book IV of the Social Code.
Children are covered until they turn 18, with longer periods in some cases set out in the statute.

When a child is not covered. A child is not insured this way if the parent related to the child who is the member's spouse or civil partner is not a member of a statutory health insurance fund, and that parent's total income regularly exceeds one twelfth of the annual earnings ceiling ("ein Zwölftel der Jahresarbeitsentgeltgrenze") and is regularly higher than the member's income.

If both parents are members. If the conditions are met more than once, the member chooses the fund.

What the parent must do. The member must report the insured family members to the responsible fund, with the information needed to carry out the family cover, and must also report later changes. The statute says the National Association of Statutory Health Insurance Funds sets a uniform procedure and uniform forms for this report.

The birth certificate. You need the birth certificate for registration with the health insurance fund, among other things. After the birth, you must register your child within 1 week with the registry office responsible for the place of birth. The registry office issues the birth certificate.

The excerpts do not say what applies if a child is not covered by family cover. Your statutory health insurance fund decides whether your baby is covered. Ask that fund about your own case.
